1) Machine Learning (Statistical Learning)
ML is the process of teaching computers to learn patterns from data and make decisions based on those patterns.

ML = input & output -> logic (Model) (ML process with input data and output and produce logic )
CS = input -> logic -> output (traditional computer science process).

Types of ML.
1) Supervised Learning (models learnined from labeled data).
  -Classification Learning (categories/classes) e.g. - email = spam or not spam , loan = yes or no (must have fixed output)
      -binary classification (output will be fixed eather yer or no , spam or not spam)
      -multi class (e.g. a sentence "this is a bad day" - output will be negative,positive or neutral) multi - class output.
  
      Classification algorithm
      -Linear Classifier
      -Logistic Regression 
      -K-Nearest Neighbour (KNN)
      -Support Vector Machine (SVM)
      -Random forest
      -XG Boost

  -Regression Learning (numerical output)
    -predict numerical output (e.g. predict delivery time , stock price forecasting, predict weight with the help of height)

    Regression algorithm
    -Linear Regression
    -Laso Regression
    -Multi-Variate Regression

2) Unsupervised Learning (models learned from unlabeled data).
    -Divide data into multiple clusters/groups
    -Data which are not in the groups/clusters called outliers/anomoly 
  
    Clustering Learning
      -Divide data into multiple groups/clusters 
    Association Learning
      -Find relationship between Different entities (market basket analysis).
      -Suggest item to buy. (e.g. buy milk + with bread suggest.)

    Unsupervised Algorithm
      -K-means Clustering
      -Hierarchical Clustering
      -PCA (Principal Component Analysis)
      -DBSCAN
  


3) Reinforcement Learning
  -In RL, an agent learns to make decisions by interacting with an environment, receiving rewards for penalties for its actions.
  -e.g. - training dogs by giving command like sit, up, run etc for rewards like foods meet.
  -agent->action->environment->rewards/penalties

RL algorithm
  -Q-Learning
  -Deep Q Networks (DQN)
  -Policy Gradient methods
  -Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)

